<name>Power Window System</name>
<para id="RM0000005DU00SX" category="J" type-id="3020C" name-id="752B4-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Window Cannot Be Operated by Driver Side Regulator Switch</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005DU00SX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000024K00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>When the IG is ON and the power window regulator master switch assembly (driver side) is operated, the power window regulator motor assembly RH (driver side) is driven. The power window regulator motor assembly RH (driver side) has a motor function, a regulator function and an ECU function.</ptxt>
<ptxt>B2311 is output when the ECU determines that the power window regulator motor assembly RH (driver side) is malfunctioning.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>If the power window regulator motor assembly RH (driver side) has been replaced with a new one, perform the registration setting of the power window system. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002FNJ005X"/>)</ptxt>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005DU00SX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000024L00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B167357J02" width="7.106578999in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
